{"full":"hf:build-small-hackathon/trikona","spaceId":"build-small-hackathon/trikona","name":"Trikona","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","modal","build-small-hackathon","best-use-of-modal","tiny-titan","off-brand","best-demo","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":3,"created":"2026-06-14T19:03:15.000Z","updated":"2026-06-15T17:31:03.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"SLEEPING","appUrl":"https://build-small-hackathon-trikona.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/trikona","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T20:29:41.982Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T20:29:41.982Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T20:29:41.982Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🔺","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Describe a geometric shape in plain language and watch it built in 3D — with its construction steps, components, and parameter space exposed.","Trikona turns a natural-language prompt (\"rotary vent with 8 vanes\", \"octahedron from 8 triangles\") into an interactive Three.js scene. A small code model (Qwen2.5-Coder 14B on Modal) generates both the geometry and a dynamic parameter schema; the entire UI — sliders, toggles, dropdowns, component list, construction steps — is built from that JSON. Nothing is hardcoded."],"features":["Demo video: In the repo or LinkedIn post","Social post: LinkedIn","Submitting for: Best Use of Modal · bonus badges Off Brand (custom UI), Tiny Titan (small model), Best Demo","Natural-language → 3D geometry via a 14B code model with JSON-mode output.","Dynamic parameter panel — controls are generated from the model's params[]."],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/trikona/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1cfe97f9831567de8bd8275a2dcdb13a751fb6eec96ac7f83144e3348b36d23b","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:32.845Z"},"overviewC